WEBVTT

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.940
All right!

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:16.860
Game, set!

00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:17.850
Yaginuma-san!

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:18.870
Io-sama!

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.650
That's Yaginuma-senpai for you.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:28.300
Everyone's making too much fuss 
over a mere practice match.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.670
Hey, Amane...

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:14.980
<b>White Hot! Team Battle</b>

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:12.730
Team Battle

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.320
A team battle?

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:19.470
It'll be Altair Torte's 
first time participating,

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:22.540
so we'll have a special briefing for you.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:24.030
So what is it?

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:28.660
I worked all night on these so that 
all of you can understand it better.

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:30.940
Wow!

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.630
Wouldn't it have been easier 
to just print handouts—

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:33.880
Team Battle

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.560
Okay!

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:38.590
Held periodically!

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:36.650
Here we go!

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.560
A paper play?

00:02:41.560 --> 00:02:43.390
I guess she just wanted to do this.

00:02:43.780 --> 00:02:48.220
We have periodic mock battles 
between the teams of the Fifth Force

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:50.650
to improve our combat capabilities.

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:54.700
The matches will be held in a special 
area within the fifth dimension,

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:57.070
and that area will be altered for each match.

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:01.240
Four teams will engage 
in a round-robin event,

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.450
and victory will be decided 
by the number of wins.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:04.450
Huh?

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.840
Round-robin event.

00:03:07.250 --> 00:03:09.030
You'll be <i>robin</i> each other of victory.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.040
I've had enough o' this!

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.290
Why Kansai dialect all of a sudden?

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:16.880
Maybe because she made a pun?

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:18.590
If you react, she wins.

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:20.760
M-Moshu...

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.140
I feel bad now!

00:03:22.610 --> 00:03:23.800
Win by KOing everyone

00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:25.940
The rules are simple.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:29.090
The team that defeats all members 
of the other team wins.

00:03:29.090 --> 00:03:30.960
All members?

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:33.020
So if even one member 
remains, we can still win.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:38.980
Moshu!

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.740
Who's that's supposed to be?

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:49.450
Use of a special Memoca

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:48.250
We'll be using a special Memoca that 
ensures you won't take much damage,

00:03:48.250 --> 00:03:49.450
so don't worry.

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.260
A special Memoca?

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:56.090
What's wrong, Io?

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.580
Do you feel sick?

00:03:57.580 --> 00:03:58.530
I can't...

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:06.140
That afro is just unfair!

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:09.760
I guess Io-chin finds afros funny.

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:10.640
Yes.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.780
So, everyone,

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:15.520
do you understand how 
the team battle works?

00:04:16.180 --> 00:04:18.400
I'm a little concerned,

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:19.650
but I do understand.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:21.400
In that case...

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:31.620
Original Comedy 
Dramatic Story

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:32.600
It's now time for the original comedy 
dramatic story I spent a month making!

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.250
Huh?

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:40.710
Yay! Yay!

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.180
Whew, that was quite an epic feature.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:53.600
I bet that was what Tierra-sensei
really wanted to do.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:58.150
The avant-garde jokes that came up 
sometimes were somewhat funny.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:00.900
Huh? I enjoyed it.

00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:05.550
Anyway, so we're having a team battle, huh?

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:08.700
It might be a good chance to 
see just how strong we are.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:13.870
Maybe there's a possibility that 
we'll be the strongest team!

00:05:14.240 --> 00:05:15.500
The strongest...

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.170
I like the sound of that.

00:05:17.170 --> 00:05:18.370
Yay!

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.290
I want to be the strongest, too!

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:24.300
Well, that aside, let's all do our best, okay?

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:26.600
Yeah!

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.380
<i>That's the match, moshu!</i>

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:51.530
<i>In the first match of the team battle,</i>

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.290
<i>Coconut Vega vs. Altair Torte,</i>

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:56.870
<i>the winner is Coconut Vega.</i>

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.880
That's how it goes the first time around.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.550
Don't get too down about it.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:06.940
Yeah...

00:06:12.930 --> 00:06:16.930
For all that they say you are, 
Yaginuma Io, you lost pretty miserably.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.310
That was pretty embarrassing.

00:06:24.050 --> 00:06:28.750
This is nothing like the way you were 
in that volleyball practice match.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:29.530
What?

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:31.740
You watched that match?

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.010
Thanks!

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:36.980
I-I was just passing by.

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:39.620
I don't care about your matches at all.

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:43.680
B-Besides, you fight as a team in volleyball,

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:47.250
so don't think you won all by yourself.

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:49.550
Yes, that's right.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.360
We won because my teammates 
tried their hardest.

00:06:54.010 --> 00:06:55.970
I'm glad you understand.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:59.140
I-I'm not really...

00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:04.300
Anyway, you'd better not hold 
anything back when you fight me!

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:05.200
Huh?

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:07.530
How could you lose so pathetically?

00:07:07.920 --> 00:07:09.820
I bet you weren't even trying!

00:07:10.580 --> 00:07:12.490
No, I really was.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:18.360
I won't accept that this is 
all Yaginuma Io can do.

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:30.260
Ranked first is Biscuit Sirius.

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:32.640
Second is Coconut Vega.

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:34.340
Third is Procyon Pudding.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:37.060
Fourth is Altair Torte.

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:40.680
Well, that was the expected result, moshu.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:42.040
Yes.

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:54.320
I think we lost because we each got flanked 
when we were separated and alone.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:57.120
It's not fair that two of them came after us!

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:02.160
I guess the plan to go man-to-man 
ended up working against us.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:04.790
It gave our opponents an advantage.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:09.740
I guess it's really all a matter of experience.

00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:17.180
No, there is a way.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:18.560
One that will work for us.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:29.870
The more experienced teams will be able to 
figure out any basic strategy we use, right?

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:35.860
So maybe we should try to outsmart them 
by using a plan they would never think of.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:37.660
I get it.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:41.790
That might be the only thing 
we can do at this point.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:43.250
Way to go, Io-chin!

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:48.180
Yeah, but I don't have an actual plan yet.

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.440
One they'd never think of, huh?

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:55.700
It looks like it's time for us

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:59.840
to utilize the super awesome 
plan I thought up in secret.

00:09:12.520 --> 00:09:13.240
Mano!

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:14.440
Crap!

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.660
<i>That's the match, moshu!</i>

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:21.830
<i>In the second day of the team battle,</i>

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:25.580
<i>the winner of the first match is Procyon Pudding.</i>

00:09:26.310 --> 00:09:27.640
Good job.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:32.170
We can't stay in third place forever.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:35.500
<i>Especially after everything I said to her...</i>

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:43.410
The next match will be Sirius, which is ranked 
first, and Torte, ranked fourth, moshu.

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:47.640
Oh, yeah, Torte said they have a special plan.

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:51.110
Well, that should be fun, moshu.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.690
<i>Now, today's second match will be</i>

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:59.620
<i>Biscuit Sirius vs. Altair Torte.</i>

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.340
<i>Time to start, moshu!</i>

00:10:05.780 --> 00:10:07.090
What's going on?

00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:07.710
What's...

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:09.370
Smoke?

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:11.700
Niho-sama...

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:15.300
So they're trying to smoke us out?

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:16.720
They sure don't think much of us.

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:28.730
We got this set up just right to blow upwind.

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:33.400
Yeah, it's good that we got 
this area for our match.

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:36.610
These live trees are perfect for making smoke.

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:42.320
They'll surely avoid going 
upwind to avoid the smoke.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:45.290
And then we'll ambush them!

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:47.030
I dub this the great

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:51.540
"Burning Campfire: Look Forward 
to the Folk Dance Later" plan!

00:10:52.640 --> 00:10:54.860
That's a needlessly long name.

00:10:55.580 --> 00:10:59.260
Yuumi-chin, it's a bit smoky, but nice idea!

00:11:01.620 --> 00:11:06.390
Altair Torte's great strategist, 
Sajima, is on the scene!

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.100
Okay, it's time to get into position.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:10.550
Roger!

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:13.680
Huh?

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:14.690
What's going on?

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.770
All the smoke is coming this way.

00:11:18.770 --> 00:11:21.700
It looks like the wind changed.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.700
This isn't supposed to happen!

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.870
My eyes burn...

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:28.250
It can't be!

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:31.580
Io-chan was supposed to have 
calculated the wind perfectly...

00:11:43.480 --> 00:11:44.600
That's...

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:50.840
Biscuit Sirius!

00:11:54.390 --> 00:11:56.890
Sorry, but this is checkmate.

00:12:01.280 --> 00:12:04.490
No way!

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:17.710
<b>1 Biscuit Sirius 
2 Coconut Vega 
3 Procyon Pudding 
4 Altair Torte</b>

00:12:19.810 --> 00:12:23.130
They were able to deal with 
our plan in an instant.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:25.730
I guess they really are the strongest.

00:12:25.730 --> 00:12:28.950
We're the weakest.

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:32.110
What should we do next, Strategist?

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:35.790
Yeah...

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:40.780
You fight as a team in volleyball.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.310
Everyone, follow me!

00:12:46.490 --> 00:12:47.950
Yeah, that's good.

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:50.790
But make sure you don't jam your fingers.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:52.250
I'm okay!

00:12:52.440 --> 00:12:54.010
Here I go!

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:57.670
Are you okay, Mana-chan?

00:12:58.400 --> 00:13:01.250
She did manage to return the ball, though.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:02.930
Guess it's a hidden talent.

00:13:02.930 --> 00:13:05.300
Come on, Yuumi-chin!

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:07.160
Sorry about that.

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:12.460
I'm tired.

00:13:12.460 --> 00:13:15.440
Exercising makes me hungry.

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:19.560
You're always thinking 
about food, Satoka-chan.

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:22.650
At least specify that it's only <i>good</i> food.

00:13:23.640 --> 00:13:26.070
So what plan are we going with this time?

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:27.410
Well...

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:32.790
I haven't thought about it at all.

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:36.160
Then why volleyball all of a sudden?

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:43.130
Well, I was thinking that teamwork would be 
the most important thing to Altair Torte.

00:13:43.570 --> 00:13:45.330
Teamwork...

00:13:45.330 --> 00:13:48.120
Volleyball is a game of teamwork, too,

00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:50.540
so I hoped I'd be able to think of something.

00:13:51.370 --> 00:13:52.930
I guess it's not that easy.

00:13:52.930 --> 00:13:54.810
No, that's not true.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:56.800
Volleyball...

00:13:56.800 --> 00:13:58.580
Teamwork...

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:00.110
That's it!

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:08.300
I am the great planner, 
Sajima the strategist.

00:14:08.300 --> 00:14:09.870
Private Yaginuma!

00:14:10.330 --> 00:14:11.160
Private?

00:14:11.660 --> 00:14:17.810
I hear your full-powered spike 
is incredibly strong.

00:14:17.810 --> 00:14:19.290
Yeah, I guess.

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:23.960
Here, here! You can ask me 
anything about Io-chin!

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:28.190
Io-chin's dynamite spike hits 150 km/h.

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:30.840
That's what it said in 
the magazine clipping.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.300
Why a clipping?

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:39.810
I save everything about you, 
whether it be online or in a newspaper.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:40.770
I see...

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:43.950
But 150 km/h is pretty fast.

00:14:43.950 --> 00:14:47.090
It'd be a bad idea to hit a 
ball that fast at someone.

00:14:47.090 --> 00:14:48.580
Yes! That's it!

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:51.660
For the team battle?

00:14:51.660 --> 00:14:53.160
You want us to use volleyball?

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:56.610
Against swords and guns?

00:14:56.610 --> 00:15:01.210
I thought we could use volleyball to enchance our teamwork, that's all.

00:15:01.930 --> 00:15:04.230
All right, quiet down.

00:15:04.230 --> 00:15:06.840
If this ball were a bomb...

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:11.600
Private Sumihara!

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:12.590
Yes?

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:14.810
As you're in charge of bombing things,

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:18.480
you should be able to carry in any 
explosives, including grenades.

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:19.680
I get it!

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.190
That sounds kinda cool!

00:15:21.510 --> 00:15:25.110
I dub this the Great Altair Storm Plan!

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:28.580
Wow! Amazing!

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:29.360
I know, right?

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:31.200
W-Wait a second.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:36.170
It's not going to explode 
the moment I spike it, right?

00:15:40.560 --> 00:15:41.210
It'll be fine!

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:44.450
Wh-What was that pause that now?

00:15:44.450 --> 00:15:45.440
Hey...

00:15:45.440 --> 00:15:47.210
Hey!

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:55.500
It's finally time to settle things,

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:56.890
Yaginuma Io!

00:15:57.320 --> 00:16:01.100
I'm not going to let you get away 
with a disappointing performance.

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:02.940
Sure. Thanks.

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:07.570
Okay, let's get this started.

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:10.740
Today's first match will be

00:16:11.040 --> 00:16:14.120
Procyon Pudding vs. Altair Torte.

00:16:14.120 --> 00:16:16.070
Begin combat, moshu!

00:16:16.930 --> 00:16:19.590
<i>Haruka and Sasa, you flank them.</i>

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:22.830
I wonder how they're going to attack.

00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:26.420
We'll crush them, no matter what they do.

00:16:30.090 --> 00:16:32.790
What's up with that outfit, moshu?

00:16:32.790 --> 00:16:35.030
I just felt like wearing it.

00:16:35.030 --> 00:16:36.310
Does it look good on me?

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:39.510
No comment, moshu.

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:43.020
Uh...

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:44.520
Are you alone?

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:46.490
Even if you're alone...

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:48.270
We won't hold back!

00:16:48.620 --> 00:16:49.730
Here I go.

00:16:53.340 --> 00:16:54.920
I got it!

00:16:56.990 --> 00:17:00.740
Each member's bio-code is 
registered with the ball, moshu.

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:02.400
Nice heading!

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:03.160
Tsubame-chan!

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:06.170
They're charging it in order.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:07.920
What's going on?

00:17:09.300 --> 00:17:10.250
Io!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:11.130
Okay!

00:17:10.250 --> 00:17:13.040
Each member is charging it up, moshu.

00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:14.720
Altair Storm!

00:17:20.840 --> 00:17:22.270
That was...

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:24.810
...a volleyball, right?

00:17:25.900 --> 00:17:27.100
Hey, ref!

00:17:27.100 --> 00:17:28.810
<i>Is that allowed?</i>

00:17:29.470 --> 00:17:31.050
Uh...

00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:32.740
No problem, moshu.

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:35.950
It was formally submitted as a weapon, moshu.

00:17:38.170 --> 00:17:40.600
Hmph! That makes things interesting!

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:41.160
Amane!

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:43.790
I'm right here.

00:17:44.510 --> 00:17:47.290
Try hitting me, Yaginuma Io!

00:17:47.680 --> 00:17:49.280
By herself?!

00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:50.540
What is she planning?

00:17:51.330 --> 00:17:52.300
Amane-san...

00:17:53.060 --> 00:17:54.050
Here I go.

00:17:56.520 --> 00:17:57.420
Here!

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.300
She's using a volleyball plan...

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:02.600
Io!

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:04.640
Altair Storm!

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:16.780
I've defeated your Altair Storm!

00:18:18.420 --> 00:18:19.450
Amane-san...

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:21.560
No way...

00:18:22.860 --> 00:18:25.450
Our finishing attack was defeated.

00:18:25.450 --> 00:18:28.330
She was able to tell which 
way the ball was flying.

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:30.580
Yaginuma Io!

00:18:31.080 --> 00:18:34.170
Your spike curves a little to the right.

00:18:35.140 --> 00:18:37.510
That's the first time I've been told that.

00:18:38.740 --> 00:18:40.790
I can't have you looking down on us.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:42.970
I've checked out all your matches.

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:45.140
My eyes know what they see!

00:18:45.840 --> 00:18:47.280
All of them?

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:49.390
Weren't you just passing by last time?

00:18:52.130 --> 00:18:53.820
Amane-chan...

00:18:53.820 --> 00:18:55.900
You like Io-san, don't you?

00:18:58.330 --> 00:19:00.130
We're in a match right now!

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:03.030
This is not the time to talk about that!

00:19:05.830 --> 00:19:07.330
What's that? What's going on?

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:12.270
It can't be...

00:19:12.270 --> 00:19:13.490
In the combat area...

00:19:13.490 --> 00:19:16.130
An O'bli signature has been detected, moshu.

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:17.300
What?

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:21.090
An O'bli!

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:23.060
And there are two of them!

00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:25.100
Huh?

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:27.810
Practice weapons won't work!

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:29.310
Amane!

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:36.940
Satoka, the ball!

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.790
R-Right!

00:19:45.440 --> 00:19:47.470
We'll buy you time,

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:48.830
so get your combat Memoca.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:50.370
Right!

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:53.840
We'll be right back, so stay safe!

00:19:53.840 --> 00:19:54.580
Yep.

00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:58.000
I'm not going to forgive you if you die!

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:02.410
Everyone, keep sending them my way.

00:20:02.410 --> 00:20:03.090
Here I go.

00:20:24.080 --> 00:20:25.110
Satoka!

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:27.850
We're out of balls...

00:20:27.850 --> 00:20:28.370
What?

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:31.240
This is bad.

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:37.810
Sorry for the wait.

00:20:37.810 --> 00:20:39.380
Leave the rest to us.

00:21:07.590 --> 00:21:08.700
We did it!

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.200
Because the O'bli appeared...

00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:25.060
...the match results were voided.

00:21:25.060 --> 00:21:28.140
I tried real hard.

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:31.030
We'll just try even harder next time.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:32.760
Yeah.

00:21:33.320 --> 00:21:36.320
Oh, Amane-san, good work.

00:21:38.020 --> 00:21:39.490
I'm impressed.

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:42.730
You have a strong enough spike 
to knock back an O'bli.

00:21:43.160 --> 00:21:44.650
Thanks.

00:21:44.650 --> 00:21:47.550
I'm happy you complimented me.

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:51.410
I-I'm not complimenting you!

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:41.020
<b>Raid! The Super SF Plan</b>

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:41.020
"Raid! The Super SF Plan."
